From 107bd77fae4e0af6e0cae73029831b9b730d1cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Furman <ifurman210@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:01:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Resolve the Vinted catalog endpoint at runtime instead of
 hardcoding it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Vinted's /api/v2/catalog/items now answers 404 with an HTML page even for a
freshly bootstrapped session, so the failure is a moved endpoint rather than an
auth problem. Users of an unrelated scraper report the same break and point at
a dedicated API host (api.vinted.<tld>/svc-catalogue/items), but nobody has
confirmed the parameter shape or headers, so nothing here is hardcoded on that
report alone.

- src/vinted/endpoints.js: known endpoint variants (api host with plain filters,
  api host with attribute_ids[...] filters, api.www host, legacy path) behind a
  single url()/extractItems() contract
- client walks the candidates, caches whichever returns items per domain, and
  re-walks when that one starts 404ing; VINTED_API_STRATEGY pins one
- distinguish "endpoint gone" (404 or an HTML body) from auth and rate-limit
  failures, so searches no longer back off behind a truncated HTML error string
- send the headers the web app sends: x-anon-id from the anon_id cookie and
  x-csrf-token scraped from the homepage meta tag
- tools/probe.mjs: run on the production IP through the residential proxy to
  measure the live contract — status, content type, JSON keys, item fields, plus
  whether the catalog HTML carries listings inline as a fallback
- /stats and poolStatus now show the resolved endpoint and CSRF state
- 4 new tests (17 total); search canonical keys are unchanged, so existing rows
  and their dedupe history stay valid

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DvFV4Tsw4NLiMvihnyrJ38
