A probe run from the production residential IP confirmed the move:
api.vinted.de/svc-catalogue/items returns listings with the catalog page's own
filter names, while the datacenter IP gets 403 on the same call.

- endpoints.js: svc-catalogue marked confirmed and tried first; each variant
  now records which header set it was confirmed with
- client sends that header set first and the other only as a fallback — the
  confirmed call sent no origin/anon-id/CSRF trio, and sending headers a
  working call omitted is its own way to get rejected; the resolved
  (endpoint, header set) pair is cached and reported by /stats
- a 403 from an unproxied session now says the datacenter IP is the problem
  instead of blaming the cookies
- normalize.js reads the svc-catalogue shape: item_box lines back the flat
  brand_title/size_title fields, which still win when present; a listing that
  parses without a price or photo logs the real key names once, so an
  unexpected shape reports itself instead of silently degrading
- docs: the proxy is no longer optional, so the "no proxy needed" row is gone
  from the cost table and the per-IP vs per-GB proxy pricing is spelled out
- 22 tests (5 new), all green

