From 105618ac5ccfa864cd5e1c5c76c39bf621a0c870 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:34:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Build catalog filters in the attribute shape and verify
 they were honoured
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An independent implementation (JakobAIOdev/Vintrack-Vinted-Monitor@3fd1ff2)
folds every id filter into attribute_ids[...] and sends x-anon-id, x-csrf-token
and x-next-app with the call. That does not contradict the probe run that
confirmed plain filter names: the confirmed URL carried only search_text and no
id filter at all, so it never exercised them.

The gap between the two is the dangerous case — the service answers 200 with
listings while dropping brand_ids, and a monitor built on that floods its topics
with the wrong brand. So:

- a query carrying id filters now leads with the attribute shape; a text-only
  search keeps the plain shape it was measured with
- the full header set adds x-next-app and the sec-fetch trio alongside the
  anon-id and CSRF token
- filtersLookHonoured() checks the answer against the filter: exact brand_id
  membership where items carry it, otherwise distinct-brand counting. A variant
  whose answer contradicts the filter is rejected and never cached, so the
  resolver settles on one that actually narrows results rather than one that
  merely returns 200
- probe-standalone.mjs runs the search with filters, without them, and in both
  parameter shapes, then states outright whether each shape narrows the results
  or was ignored
- 25 tests, all green

