From 4c9def4d4ea21d4d185345523f93200f3517c54a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:44:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Keep the plain filter shape away from filtered searches,
 and fix a probe crash
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured on the production IP: a search pinned to brand 344976 in the plain
shape came back with an adidas listing, while the attribute shape returned a
filtered set. The plain shape accepts *_ids and ignores them.

- strategies are now (host, filter shape) pairs, and a query carrying id filters
  is offered the attribute-shaped variants only. The plain shape is not a
  fallback for such a query — it is a wrong answer, and no listings beats
  listings of the wrong brand. Two api hosts keep it from being a single point
  of failure.
- probe-standalone.mjs gains the verdict check (it was added there last commit;
  the copy on the server predates it) plus a direct brand test: each run reports
  how many returned items actually carry the requested brand_id, and a run whose
  answer holds more brands than were asked for is called out as ignored.
- fix a crash in the probe's CONNECT tunnel: a rejected proxy connection left
  its socket undestroyed, which later emitted ECONNRESET with no listener and
  killed the run mid-matrix. Verified by running the probe with every request
  failing — it now completes all sections and prints the report.
- 26 tests, all green

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DvFV4Tsw4NLiMvihnyrJ38
