From 828bbcc081e55e75e740e423ad176c7fcd8ebfe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:50:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Mark the attribute filter shape as confirmed, warn when
 no proxy is set
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The attribute shape was verified against the live catalog from the production
IP: the brand filter is honoured. The note in endpoints.js now says measured
rather than reported, and TECH.md records both halves of the move — the path and
the filter names — since the silent filter drop is the more dangerous of the two.

Also warn at boot when PROXIES is empty: the catalog answers 403 to datacenter
IPs, so an unproxied deployment fails every search, and that should be visible
