From 7718cde24284c95c2b68f312215232c9c3bc4834 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:59:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Key the endpoint cache by query class, not by domain
 alone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reported from production: a text-only search resolved to the plain shape, and
the next brand-filtered search on the same domain reused that cached choice —
so its brand filter was dropped and the topic filled with other brands again.
candidatesFor() prepended the cached pair unconditionally, without checking that
the pair was even a legal candidate for the query at hand, which put the plain
shape in front of a filtered query the ordering had deliberately excluded.

- the cache key is now `<domain>|text` or `<domain>|filtered`, so the two query
  classes resolve independently
- independently of the key, a remembered pair is only used when it is still
  among the candidates allowed for this query; anything else is treated as stale
- filtersLookHonoured() also checks catalog_ids where listings carry catalog_id,
  so the last line of defence is not brand-only
- /stats reports both resolutions per domain
- two regression tests, both verified to fail against the previous code
- 29 tests, all green

