From a3ca0f219396d4ef2505120ae4123d9991f218dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:19:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Auto-create forum topics, translate the interface,
 survive supergroup upgrades
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four changes to how the bot is used.

Auto topic creation: picking a Topics-enabled group while adding a search now
offers "Create topic <name>", which calls createForumTopic and binds the search
to the returned thread in one step. Nobody has to open the group, make a topic
and run /bind inside it. Existing topics and "whole group" stay available, and a
missing can-manage-topics right is reported with the reason rather than failing
silently.

Languages: every user-visible string moved into src/i18n/locales/{en,ru,de,uk},
addressed by key, with English as the fallback. The language is seeded from the
Telegram client locale on first contact and switchable via /lang or the menu.
Menu buttons are matched in every language at once, so a user who switches mid
session does not end up with dead buttons. Two tests keep the dictionaries from
drifting: identical key sets, identical placeholders per key.

Supergroup migration: enabling Topics upgrades a group and Telegram issues a new
chat id, after which every send failed forever with "group chat was upgraded to
a supergroup chat" until someone re-ran /bind. Both signals are now handled —
the migrate_to_chat_id service message, and the same id echoed inside the send
error for an upgrade that happened while the bot was offline. Searches and the
chat row move in one transaction, the owner is told, and the listing that
triggered the error is re-delivered to the new chat.

Button label: the listing button reads "URL".

- schema gains users.lang, applied to existing databases by an idempotent
  column check at startup
- 32 tests (10 new), all green

